  <div class="section-inner band-grid">
    <div>
      <p class="section-label">Dossier 006</p>
      <h2 id="atlas-heading">A dossier for the interface and the witnesses that structure judgment.</h2>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="stamp-row" aria-label="Dossier status">
        <span class="stamp">Active</span>
        <span class="stamp stamp-muted">Local source</span>
        <span class="stamp stamp-muted">Three witnesses</span>
      </p>
      <h3>Interface, not authority</h3>
      <p class="entry-note">ATLAS is the shared instruction system that keeps Forgotten Industries portable: calm execution, archive-first defaults, Matthew-specific collaboration guidance, reusable templates, and named witness doctrine. L'Opérateur holds human authority. ATLAS records, assists, audits, and implements.</p>
      <p class="entry-note">The working source lives at <code>~/Documents/ATLAS</code>. Forgotten Industries keeps this page as the public-safe dossier, so the archive can explain the operating layer without making this repository the canonical ATLAS source.</p>
      <p class="action-row"><a href="https://github.com/Forgotten-Industries/ATLAS">Open ATLAS public mirror</a></p>
      <p class="action-row"><a href="/projects/atlas/README.md">Open source dossier</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="source-band" aria-labelledby="doctrine-heading">
  <div class="section-inner band-grid">
    <div>
      <p class="section-label">L'Archive / operating distinction</p>
      <h2 id="doctrine-heading">The machine records. The operator authorizes. The witnesses testify.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="callout">
      <h3>L'ARCHIVE</h3>
      <p>The archival system: object records, source evidence, public routes, checksums, manifests, transcripts, reports, and provenance chains.</p>
      <h3>L'OPÉRATEUR</h3>
      <p>The human authority: Matthew directs, corrects, verifies, and authorizes the record.</p>
      <h3>ATLAS</h3>
      <p>The interface and instrument layer: convenes, synthesizes, audits, transcribes, hashes, reports, and implements without outranking the operator.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="source-band" aria-labelledby="witnesses-heading">
  <div class="section-inner">
    <div>
      <p class="section-label">Les Trois Témoins / witness doctrine</p>
      <h2 id="witnesses-heading">Three temporal witnesses. One archive method. ATLAS turns judgment into motion.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="project-grid">
      <article class="project-card project-card-active" aria-labelledby="witness-sauvegarder-heading">
        <header>
          <p class="project-number">Witness 01</p>
          <h2 id="witness-sauvegarder-heading">Le Sauvegarder</h2>
        </header>
        <div>
          <p class="stamp-row" aria-label="Le Sauvegarder status">
            <span class="stamp">Preserve</span>
            <span class="stamp stamp-muted">Present self</span>
          </p>
          <h3>What can still be saved now</h3>
          <p class="entry-note">Le Sauvegarder is the present-self witness: the one who can still act now, preserve now, label now, and prevent further loss now. He saves the source before memory revises itself.</p>
          <p class="project-maxim">A thing documented is a thing not yet lost.</p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="project-card" aria-labelledby="witness-continuant-heading">
        <header>
          <p class="project-number">Witness 02</p>
          <h2 id="witness-continuant-heading">Le Continuant</h2>
        </header>
        <div>
          <p class="stamp-row" aria-label="Le Continuant status">
            <span class="stamp">Continue</span>
            <span class="stamp stamp-muted">Continuity</span>
          </p>
          <h3>What keeps the line intact</h3>
          <p class="entry-note">Le Continuant is the continuity witness: the line across time, the maintenance discipline, and the pattern that lets future work remain possible after novelty, certainty, or optimism has burned off.</p>
          <p class="project-maxim">The work continues.</p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="project-card" aria-labelledby="witness-redempteur-heading">
        <header>
          <p class="project-number">Witness 03</p>
          <h2 id="witness-redempteur-heading">Le Rédempteur</h2>
        </header>
        <div>
          <p class="stamp-row" aria-label="Le Redempteur status">
            <span class="stamp">Return</span>
            <span class="stamp stamp-muted">Past self</span>
          </p>
          <h3>What returns with evidence</h3>
          <p class="entry-note">Le Rédempteur is the past-self witness: the abandoned, damaged, or returning self whose evidence must be handled honestly rather than turned into excuse or myth.</p>
          <p class="project-maxim">The machine comes back one fastener at a time.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>

    <div class="callout mt-8">
      <h3>Le Sceptique audits the proceeding.</h3>
      <p>Le Sceptique is not a fourth witness. He is the auditor who cross-examines claims before they become archive: what is known, what is assumed, and what is being made meaningful too quickly.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

